  "articleBody": "When you're tackling a home accessibility project, it's easy to overlook a few things, but avoiding common pitfalls can save you a lot of headaches later. One big mistake is not checking your whole home for thresholds, stairs, and tight turning clearances – it’s not just about one room, right? Another frequent error is only thinking about today's needs and not considering what you might need down the line. Future-proofing your home means fewer remodels later. And please, don't skimp on contractor due diligence! Always ask for references and proof of insurance to make sure you're working with a reputable professional. Also, forgetting structural backing for grab bars is a common safety miss. If you're using outside funding, make sure you get formal authorization before any work starts, otherwise, you might not get reimbursed. These projects can be complex, so if you're feeling unsure, it’s a good idea to reach out to an experienced contractor like HH Remodeling LLC who can guide you through the process.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}